-- title:
--   Path integrals modulo the lattice of edge jumps
-- statement:
--   Let $F$ be a field with a $\mathbb{C}$-algebra structure satisfying `IsCurveOver ℂ F` (principal divisors, finite residue extensions, and $\Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ free of rank one) and essentially of finite type, whose place space $\mathrm{Place}\,\mathbb{C}\,F$ carries a Hausdorff charted analytic one-dimensional complex manifold structure; assume $F$ contains a transcendental $x$ with $F$ finite over $\mathbb{C}(x)$ (`hfg`), and that every $f \neq 0$ reads, in the chart at each place $v$, as a meromorphic function whose order at the centre is $v.\mathrm{ord}\,f$ (`hF`). Let $\mathcal{D}$ be a cell dissection of $F$, $\kappa$ a finite type, and $\eta : \kappa \to \Omega_{F/\mathbb{C}}$ differentials with $Q.\mathrm{ordDifferential}(\eta_i) \ge 0$ at every place $Q$. Suppose given, for each cell $C$, an open $V\,C \subseteq \mathbb{C}$ with $K_C \subseteq V\,C \subseteq$ the target of the chart $\zeta_C$, and functions $\Psi_{i,C}$ with $\Psi_{i,C}' = \mathrm{coeffIn}\,\zeta_C\,\eta_i$ everywhere on $V\,C$; suppose further that for each edge $e$, writing $\langle C_+,k_+\rangle$ and $\langle C_-,k_-\rangle$ for the arcs carrying $e$ with orientation `true` and `false`, the difference $\Psi_{i,C_+}(\mathrm{loop}_{C_+}(s)) - \Psi_{i,C_-}(\zeta_{C_-}(\mathrm{bdry}_{C_+}(s)))$ is the constant $J_{e,i}$ for all $s$ in the parameter interval of the arc $k_+$. Finally let $\delta$ be a path from $P$ to $P'$, let each $g_i$ be a primitive of $\eta_i$ along $\delta$ in the sense of `IsPrimitiveAlong` (locally $g_i(t) = \Phi(\text{chart}(\delta t))$ for a local primitive $\Phi$ of the read differential), and let $P \in (\mathcal{D}.\mathrm{cell}\,C).\mathrm{carrier}$, $P' \in (\mathcal{D}.\mathrm{cell}\,C').\mathrm{carrier}$. Then there exist integers $n_e$, one family independent of $i$, such that for every $i$ $$\bigl(g_i(1) - g_i(0)\bigr) - \bigl(\Psi_{i,C'}(\zeta_{C'}P') - \Psi_{i,C}(\zeta_C P)\bigr) = \sum_e n_e\, J_{e,i}.$$
--
--   This is the statement that a path integral of a family of everywhere-regular differentials agrees with the difference of the cell primitives at the endpoints up to an integral combination of the edge jumps; for a closed path with $C = C'$ it says that the period vector lies in the lattice generated by the jump vectors $J_e$. It feeds the reciprocity statement [`AlgebraicCurve.exists_loops_pathIntegral_reciprocity_raw`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.exists_loops_pathIntegral_reciprocity_raw) for period integrals over loops, and it uses the local computation [`AlgebraicCurve.coeffIn_local_calculus`](thm.html#AlgebraicCurve.coeffIn_local_calculus) relating `coeffIn` to the chart-read differential.
